attestations/decisions_DR-2026-06-10-synthesis-model-floor.json:10:      "reason": "This DR clarifies the scope of rule #2 (capability floor vs brand pin) but writes no best_practice_synthesis. No synthesis content is authored; the facts/judgment split is preserved verbatim."
attestations/decisions_DR-2026-06-10-synthesis-model-floor.json:28:      "reason": "The weak-band delta concerns which cells may be called best practice, not who authors synthesis. This DR's capability-floor rule ('Opus-class or above') is untouched. Verdict unchanged."
attestations/decisions_DR-2026-07-12-evidence-cell-state-schema-reconciliation.json:28:   "reason": "The weak-band delta changes how a regulatory_stratum_only cell RENDERS (weak-band best practice), not the four-state schema or the flag itself. Schema-reconciliation decision unchanged; verdict CLEAN stands."
attestations/decisions_DR-2026-07-13-attestation-rule-identifier-registry-gap.json:30:  "independent_reviewer_counterclaim": "An outside reviewer would observe: (a) this DR's Category A/B split, and its claim that all 8 identifiers are 'genuine, load-bearing concepts,' rests entirely on reading the identifiers' own self-descriptions in attestations that this same project's sessions authored -- it is not independent evidence that e.g. 'best-practice-synthesis-routing' was ever a deliberately-chosen stable identifier versus an ad-hoc phrase one session happened to reuse six times; (b) the 'do not rewrite historical attestations' argument in item 2, while consistent with the migrations' forward-only convention, is itself a policy choice this DR makes on the owner's behalf rather than surfacing as a genuinely open question -- a reviewer might reasonably prefer the rename-to-canonical path for the 3 Category-B variants precisely because it would make skill-registry.md's identifier space cleaner going forward; (c) no attempt was made to check whether any of the 8 identifiers appear in non-attestation project files (skill files, PI text) where a canonical definition might already exist and simply wasn't searched for. Counter: (a) six-times-reused-with-consistent-meaning across a 3-week span is a reasonable practical bar for 'not ad-hoc,' though not proof of deliberate registration; (b) the DR names this exact fork in its closing section precisely so a reviewer can override it; (c) is a fair gap -- a more thorough pass would grep skill files and PI text for each of the 8 strings before concluding no canonical source exists, and this DR does not claim to have done so.",
attestations/decisions_DR-2026-07-13-value-genealogy-and-derivation-handshake.json:33:   "reason": "Weak-band material scope includes value-genealogy, but the delta (code-only = flagged weak best practice) does not alter the genealogy/derivation-handshake design this DR ratified. Verdict unchanged."
attestations/decisions_DR-2026-07-20-evidence-architecture-weighted-strength-reconciliation.json:15:  "independent_reviewer_counterclaim": "A reviewer could argue no DR is warranted: the evidence-architecture.md:4 precedence clause already makes tier-system.md §8 govern, so the divergence is inert until evidence-architecture.md is next edited, and opening a DR manufactures work the freeze forbids. The counter is narrow but real — assess_cell.py's v_best_practice still mechanically excludes regulatory-stratum-only cells, so code and §8 already disagree at render time; whether that matters before any such cell is actually rendered is itself the open question, which this DR routed to the owner rather than deciding. best-practice-synthesis-routing and evidence-verification-gate-for-synthesis were NOT exercised by this framing DR (no synthesis written, no source cited).",
attestations/decisions_DR-2026-07-20-intra-category-cross-test.json:27:   "reason": "Grounded at the person-mode sweep; the weak-band delta (best-practice rendering) is material by scope. Re-reviewed: the intra-category cross-test methodology is unaffected by the rendering change. Verdict unchanged."
attestations/decisions_DR-2026-07-21-evidence-architecture-option-a-execution.json:14:  "bias_direction": "Executing a canonical-doctrine amendment under an owner one-liner ('Option A … flagged as weak') gives the author wide latitude to shape ratified text, and interpretive resolutions (weak ○ band even with T4/T5 present; no code x person anchoring; state machine untouched; contested-direction safeguard) were decided by the author, not the owner — each could be a convenient reading that minimizes downstream engine work while presenting as faithful execution. The doc was also deliberately advanced ahead of the engine, which lets the author claim the doctrine is 'done' while the mechanically-enforced invariant (I3) still enforces the repealed form. best-practice-synthesis-routing and evidence-verification-gate-for-synthesis were NOT exercised (no synthesis written, no source cited); scope narrowed to the one rule that fired per check 8.",
attestations/decisions_DR-2026-07-21-evidence-architecture-option-a-execution.json:15:  "independent_reviewer_counterclaim": "The strongest objection: Option A blesses 'best practice' wording for code-only cells, which directly contradicts mission-and-epistemics.md doctrine #2 ('a best-practice claim derived solely from code consensus is in error') — the deepest doctrine, and best-practice-synthesis-routing is registered (DR-2026-07-13) as exactly 'the best-practice-vs-code-consensus routing rule (mission doctrine #2)', so marking it NOT-FIRED on a narrow 'writes no synthesis row' reading understates that this DR rewrites that rule's doctrinal substrate. The mission reconciliation is therefore escalated to the owner (not applied) because it is the owner's identity statement and editing it rotates the 373255e doctrine-sha every attestation pins; until the owner amends the mission, the precedence clause leaves a residual tension. The doc-leads-code divergence is mitigated (explicit, directional ENGINE-LAG markers; no RSO cell renders until the engine follow-up lands) but is real and the owner may prefer to gate the doc amendment on the engine work.",
