attestations/sessions_session_2026-07-20-anchor-correctness-sweep.json:30: "independent_reviewer_counterclaim": "A reviewer could argue that even scalar corrections (e.g. jurisdiction reassignments) encode modeling choices and should not be auto-applied without per-row human sign-off. Response: jurisdiction/language/year/count fields do not affect anchor status or best-practice weight, each was adversarially upheld against a live retrieval, each records its evidence in verification_note, and all are forward-only reversible; the consequential tier/type and identity-string changes were explicitly withheld for exactly the human-review reason raised.",
attestations/sessions_session_2026-07-20-anchor-correctness-sweep.json:39:   "reason": "Weak-band material by anchor/best-practice scope. The sweep verified anchor SOURCES (T1/T2/Co); the weak-band rendering change does not alter those source verifications. Verdict unchanged."
attestations/sessions_session_2026-07-20-bathroom-typology-global-south-rederivation.json:15:   "reason": "Tiered every source strictly by governance/tier-system.md: Sprouse 2024 placed at T2 as an sr_meta (§2 t2>t3), the two Indonesian primary studies at T3, the JMP monitoring report at T4 per the WHO/UNICEF-guidance convention (cf. REF-00125/00187/00215), and the three national accessibility codes (NBR 9050, Permen PUPR 14/2017, MLIT 建築設計標準) at T6 code-floor. Applied §3 explicitly: the T6 codes and the T4 JMP report are recorded as code-baseline / scope citations that do NOT anchor a best-practice claim, and the squat-toilet specification gap was left open rather than resolved by code-convergence."
attestations/sessions_session_2026-07-20-bathroom-typology-global-south-rederivation.json:29: "bias_direction": "The pull on a retracted-slice re-derivation is completion bias: reinstating the prior synthesis's rich named-source list wholesale to move the grade fastest, which would silently re-import whatever fabricated or drifted citations caused the retraction. Bounded by treating every prior lead as guilty until a live tool call proved it, dropping the two that failed (Solano review; the phantom 93-study SR), and letting the slice land at PARTIAL with best_practice_synthesis still BLOCKED rather than papering the squat-specification gap.",
attestations/sessions_session_2026-07-20-bathroom-typology-global-south-rederivation.json:30: "independent_reviewer_counterclaim": "A reviewer could argue the shared-sanitation SR (Sprouse 2024) is overstated as a Cluster-4 anchor because disability is a sub-theme, not its focus, so tagging it T2 inflates the slice's best-practice depth. Response: it is cited for its shared-sanitation user-preference synthesis (privacy, lighting, safety) that genuinely informs the communal-facility cluster, and the relevance note explicitly records that disability is a named vulnerability rather than the review's primary subject, so the anchor is scoped, not inflated.",
attestations/sessions_session_2026-07-20-grey-noneng-audit.json:39:   "reason": "Grey-literature non-English audit; weak-band material by best-practice scope. It re-tagged mis-tagged academic sources; unaffected by the rendering delta. Verdict unchanged."
attestations/sessions_session_2026-07-20-retracted-slice-rederivation-batch.json:15:   "reason": "Applied governance/tier-system.md §3 (convergence-not-evidence) as the load-bearing doctrine: jurisdiction-matrix-accessibility-standards was left graded D-double-dagger (code-floor/convergence-only, T4x4 T6x10) and its BPC banner states explicitly that a matrix of statutory codes carries no best-practice anchor by nature, rather than manufacturing a T1/T2 anchor to lift the grade. WHO APS15's 110 kg and the ADA/BS 8300 code figures were tagged as procurement/code floors, not best-practice anchors, on the grab-bar slice. Each re-linked source kept its corpus tier; none was re-tiered to flatter a slice."
attestations/sessions_session_2026-07-25-energy-conservation-rest-points-seating-b2.json:11:  "best-practice-synthesis-routing",
