decisions/DR-2026-05-24-best-practice-supersession-protocol.md:1:# DR-2026-05-24 — Best-Practice Supersession Protocol
decisions/DR-2026-05-24-best-practice-supersession-protocol.md:4:**Authored:** 2026-05-25 (session_2026-05-23-bpc-rewrite-phase-b-closure)
decisions/DR-2026-05-24-best-practice-supersession-protocol.md:12:PI standing rule #6 (canonical workplan) and mission doctrinal commitments 2, 3, and 5 hold that best practice for the guidebook is determined by the evidence hierarchy, not by code consensus or by whatever evidence happened to be in the corpus when a slug was first scoped. The Phase B citation-mining protocol (skill: `citation-miner`) surfaces references that cite or are cited by an anchor source — a citation-graph operation. It does **not** check whether each anchor source remains the best current evidence for the parameter × population × outcome it supports.
decisions/DR-2026-05-24-best-practice-supersession-protocol.md:14:A slug closed under the old citation_mining_complete=1 bar can have all anchor sources protocol-mined and still rest on stale best evidence — for example, citing the 2010 ANSI/ASA S12.60 revision when a 2024 revision exists, or citing 2018-era systematic reviews when 2024 Cochrane or JBI work supersedes the synthesis. That is exactly the failure mode mission doctrinal commitment 2 prohibits ("a best-practice claim derived solely from code consensus is in error" — and by symmetric reasoning, a best-practice claim derived from a *superseded* Tier-3 source is also in error, because the operative evidence hierarchy includes a temporal dimension).
decisions/DR-2026-05-24-best-practice-supersession-protocol.md:59:2. **Semiannual sweep** — Across the full corpus, every six months, run a temporal-pass supersession check: for every anchor source whose last_checked_date is older than the sweep horizon, re-run the supersession search filtered to publication date > last_checked_date. Sweep dates: 2026-12-01 (first post-DR sweep, ~6 months after this DR) and every 6 months thereafter. The sweep cadence is itself a methodological declaration — between sweeps, the BPC's evidence base is correct as of the last sweep, not as of "today."
decisions/DR-2026-05-24-best-practice-supersession-protocol.md:85:3. **Grounds best practice in evidence hierarchy?** Yes — supersession searches are tier-prioritized; a Tier-1 candidate supersedes a Tier-3 anchor regardless of recency, and within the same tier, recency tie-breaks.
decisions/DR-2026-05-24-best-practice-supersession-protocol.md:96:1. **This DR** at `decisions/DR-2026-05-24-best-practice-supersession-protocol.md`.
decisions/DR-2026-05-24-best-practice-supersession-protocol.md:117:- governance/mission-and-epistemics.md doctrinal commitment 2 (best practice from evidence hierarchy, not code consensus)
decisions/DR-2026-05-24-best-practice-supersession-protocol.md:119:- governance/mission-and-epistemics.md §Evidence-state machine for best-practice claims
decisions/DR-2026-05-24-best-practice-supersession-protocol.md:121:- workplan/bpc-rewrite-workplan-2026-05-11.md §B.11 (citation mining)
decisions/DR-2026-05-26-gap-driven-mining-protocol.md:126:3. **Grounds best practice in evidence hierarchy?** Yes — search matrix is tier-prioritized per gap pattern; discoveries enter the evidence base only after rule #10 verification.
decisions/DR-2026-05-26-gap-driven-mining-protocol.md:169:- `governance/mission-and-epistemics.md` doctrinal commitment 2 (best practice from evidence hierarchy, not code consensus)
decisions/DR-2026-05-26-gap-driven-mining-protocol.md:177:- `decisions/DR-2026-05-24-best-practice-supersession-protocol.md` (companion DR; same append-only-per-attempt design pattern)
decisions/DR-2026-06-10-synthesis-model-floor.md:6:**Relates to:** PI v10.14 standing rule #2 (best-practice-synthesis routing); `skills/multilingual-research_SKILL.md` and sibling skill headers (model pins); Stage 4.3 execution plan §4 Pass 2.
decisions/DR-2026-06-10-synthesis-model-floor.md:12:PI standing rule #2 states: "Sonnet does NOT write `best_practice_synthesis` — only Opus." The skill headers concur, pinning specific model strings ("Sonnet 4.6 (search) · Opus 4.6 (best_practice_synthesis)"). These were authored when Opus was the most capable model available to the project.
decisions/DR-2026-06-10-synthesis-model-floor.md:18:1. **Rule #2 is a capability floor, expressed as "Opus-class or above."** Any model at or above Opus's synthesis capability may write `best_practice_synthesis`. Claude Fable 5 (Mythos-class, above Opus) satisfies the floor.
decisions/DR-2026-07-12-evidence-architecture-unification-impact-appendix.md:25:**Governance/references.** Beyond the canonical six: `references/project-standards.md` (**highest-risk single file** — standing-rules register agents load, restating the superseded ladder as RULEs + 16 Mode P/S uses; feeds `doctrine_recheck.py`); `governance/pre-stage-a-decisions.md` L49/L81 (OLD stated threshold); `architecture/schema-spec.md` L78–98 (**wrong co1_source_type enum + phantom 'co1-collaborator' evidence_type — (c) hard conflict**); `references/global-reference-registry.md` (hybrid "Co-1/N" labels defeating tier+type encoding); (b)-colliding: `adversarial-use-framework.md`, `legal-regulatory.md` (also L29 lumps T4–5 into best-practice synthesis — (a) conflict), `population-taxonomy.md`, `armature_v4_resolutions.md`, `armature_v4_integration.md` (adds a 4th vocabulary, "Tier A/B/C"), `jurisdiction-philosophy.md` L75 (mild (a) conflict).
decisions/DR-2026-07-12-evidence-architecture-unification.md:14:Maximum-effort review (this session) found the question ~80% answered by existing doctrine — decision D-D (`evidence-methodology.md` §§1.4–1.7), the role layer (`armature_v4.md` §4.5), the audience structure (`audience-priority.md`), and the weighting-profile design (`workplan/best-practices-assessment-system.md` §5) — but the answer was (a) scattered across six-plus documents with no unifying statement, (b) obscured by a vocabulary collision in which "Tier 1/Tier 2" name design modes in `mission-and-epistemics.md` commitment 4 and evidence tiers everywhere else, plus a third "Mode P/Mode S" vocabulary, (c) un-ratified (four keystone DRs PROPOSED), and (d) unbuilt (`evidence_cell_state` = 0 rows). Adversarial review then found six genuine gaps at the edges of the existing resolution, two of them verified bugs in `schemas/directness.py` and one a latent doctrine–code contradiction; the operational pilot subsequently surfaced two more (G7, G8 — see revision history v2), for eight ratifiable gap items in total.
decisions/DR-2026-07-12-evidence-architecture-unification.md:22:**Problem.** `evidence-methodology.md` §2.3 allows a cell to reach `provisional` on T4–6 convergence alone, and §3.4 supplies rendering language for it, while `tier-system.md` §3 and `schemas/directness.py` (NON-ANCHORING) forbid exactly that stratum from anchoring best-practice claims. The `code_floor_only` flag (migration 026) covers only the T6-only case, so a T4/T5-only cell passes `v_best_practice`; the policymaker weighting profile up-weights exactly this stratum. This is the mechanism by which a policymaker rendering could launder code-convergence into best practice.
decisions/DR-2026-07-12-evidence-architecture-unification.md:24:**Recommendation.** (a) **Scale-tagging:** every determination is tagged with the design scale its claim speaks to; T4–6-only determinations are Universal-Mode regulatory determinations, never rendered as best practice in any register. (b) **Flag extension:** `regulatory_stratum_only` (T4–6-only) supersedes/extends `code_floor_only` (T6-only); `v_best_practice` excludes it. (c) **Re-graining rule:** a T4/T5 source escapes GRAIN_CODE (→ GRAIN_AGGREGATE) only when its own evidence basis is documented traceable to T1/T2, provenance recorded — operationalizing the "if the standard itself rests on T1/T2 evidence" clause already in `tier-system.md` §1.
decisions/DR-2026-07-12-evidence-architecture-unification.md:52:**Recommendation.** Ratify advocacy-brief as a use-pattern within the disabled-person primary audience (extendable to carers, DPO staff): emphasis = code-vs-best-practice delta + rights framing + citable evidence strength. Amends `audience-priority.md` (use-pattern table) post-ratification; no change to the four-audience structure or priority rules.
decisions/DR-2026-07-12-evidence-architecture-unification.md:84:A full-repo impact sweep (code / database / book / site / skills / governance) was run this session; the complete map is `decisions/DR-2026-07-12-evidence-architecture-unification-impact-appendix.md`. Summary of directions: **code** — `schemas/directness.py` gains additive per-`rule_version` paths (G1/G2/G3/G6); `validate_evidence_state.py` check extended (G1b); generators consume the register map when audience rendering ships. **Database** — one follow-on migration (`regulatory_stratum_only`; `weighting_profile` seeding); no change to applied history. **Book (`parts/v10/`)** — vocabulary-normalization edits (Item V execution list); any prose stating T4–6 convergence as best practice is a defect on current doctrine already, listed in the appendix. **Site** — population/spec page generators unaffected until they render determinations; then bound by I1–I5. **Skills** — hierarchy-teaching skills (e.g., `guidebook-auditor_SKILL.md`) amended in lock-step per the tier-system.md §6 precedent. **Governance** — four prose amendments listed below; no ratified doctrine is contradicted, three PROPOSED DRs are extended compatibly.
decisions/DR-2026-07-12-evidence-architecture-unification.md:93:6. Follow-on migration 027: `regulatory_stratum_only` column + `v_best_practice` exclusion + `weighting_profile` seed rows for the four audience use-patterns + advocacy-brief.
decisions/DR-2026-07-12-evidence-architecture-unification.md:117:- v1.1 (same day): (a) full-repo impact sweep completed → `…-impact-appendix.md`; execution section extended with items 8–13 (project-standards.md, stated-threshold triangle, MODE-S-ONLY migration, SHA-pin hygiene, PopulationCode drift). (b) Pilot executed end-to-end on the working-copy DB: 7 cells, deterministic (byte-identical double run), validator clean, 6/6 validator mutations + 4/4 register-invariant mutations fired. (c) **Self-caught defect via I3's strictness:** the first register-map draft used "best practice" inside negations on regulatory-stratum rows; the checker flagged it; wording corrected in renderer + `evidence-architecture.md` §6 — I3 is deliberately a total phrase ban.
decisions/DR-2026-07-12-evidence-architecture-unification.md:118:- v2 (same day): **independent adversarial review returned 18 findings (1 CRITICAL, 8 MAJOR); all corrected.** Highlights, with the fixed artifacts as evidence: (1) CRITICAL — the pilot's regulatory-stratum cell WAS in `v_best_practice` (026's view excludes only `code_floor_only`); the replay artifact now amends the view (marker-based interim; migration 027 adds the column) and the exclusion is verified by query. (2) Manifest claimed unit tests that did not exist — `scripts/tests/test_assess_cell_pilot.py` now makes the claims true (and immediately caught a real jurisdiction-distinctness bug in the richness check). (3) The G-03×SCI gap text asserted corpus-level evidence absence when the absence was slug-scoped — gap descriptions are now explicitly slug-scoped, item-relevant sibling-slug evidence acknowledged. (4) §2.8 verification machinery implemented (`has_unverified_sources`/`all_sources_disqualified`). (5) Three demonstrated I1–I5 bypasses closed: tuple-class recomputation + tier-basis-marker consistency + DB cross-check (`--db`), I3 synonym lexicon, I5 inflation lexicon over full rendering bodies; all added to the checker's selftest. (6) Register-map delta claims ("exceeds the statutory floor") removed until value extraction supports them. (7) "Legal minimum" labels corrected — `jurisdictional_values` stores voluntary standards alongside statutory codes (new execution item 15); all floors rendered, no silent truncation. (8) B-10's `standard_eb`@T2 anchoring is now DR-flagged as item G7; `tier_basis` describes the governing set only, supporting strata listed separately, `derivation_sha` cell-scoped. (9) `pending_assessment` rendering DR-flagged as item G8. (10-18) citation fixes (§3 item 6; stated/provisional-scoped anti-hallucination sentence), `scripts/audit/matrix_consistency.py` created, mapping-v2 JBI/SIGN/GRADE corrections + carried-forward v1 content restored, Co-1 solo-authorship limit rendered in every register, richness rationale names its unchecked clauses, population-match rows attributed per population, pilot DB stamped user_version=26, engine bumped to rule_version pilot-2. Also reconciled with PR #3 (consolidation sweep, merged upstream mid-review): two additional PROPOSED DRs join the ratification roster (now 13), and this change-set adds one expected line to the sweep's schema-drift audit (pilot renderer → `jurisdictional_values`, resolved when 026 applies).
decisions/DR-2026-07-12-evidence-cell-state-schema-reconciliation.md:6:- Affects (if ratified): `scripts/migrations/026_reconcile_evidence_cell_state.sql`, `scripts/migrations/data_20260712150000_jurisdictional-values-backfill.sql`, `scripts/validate_evidence_state.py`, `workplan/best-practices-assessment-system.md`
decisions/DR-2026-07-12-evidence-cell-state-schema-reconciliation.md:11:Two incompatible schemas exist for `evidence_cell_state`, the empty table meant to hold the project's central per-cell best-practice determination:
decisions/DR-2026-07-12-evidence-cell-state-schema-reconciliation.md:15:**B. `workplan/best-practices-assessment-system.md` §4 (2026-06-22; explicitly "sketch; finalize as migration 026," never built):** keyed on `(slug, population, jurisdiction)`. Convergence is a flat `convergence` enum column with no directness distinction. Adds real, valuable capability schema A lacks: `governing_refs` (anti-hallucination), `rule_version` + `derivation_sha` (staleness detection), `tier_basis`, `code_floor_only`, `value_range`, and a `falsification` condition.
decisions/DR-2026-07-12-evidence-cell-state-schema-reconciliation.md:22:2. **Do not add a `jurisdiction` dimension to this table at all.** `governance/tier-system.md`'s corridor-width worked example is explicit that "best practice" (evidence-anchored, e.g. 2440mm) and "regulatory floor" (jurisdiction-specific code convergence, e.g. 1800mm) are different *kinds* of claim, and that treating jurisdiction-convergence as best-practice evidence is the named failure mode this doctrine exists to prevent. Baking jurisdiction into `evidence_cell_state`'s identity — even as a nullable/sentinel column — puts a jurisdiction-specific dimension inside a table whose determination is supposed to be jurisdiction-agnostic by definition. Instead:
decisions/DR-2026-07-12-evidence-cell-state-schema-reconciliation.md:25:5. **Add schema B's provenance/reproducibility columns**: `tier_basis`, `governing_refs` (JSON array, `CHECK (... json_valid(...))`), `rule_version`, `derivation_sha`, `code_floor_only`, `falsification_condition`. Replace B's unstructured `value_range TEXT` with **structured** `value_min REAL, value_max REAL, value_unit TEXT` — matching the numeric/unit convention `jurisdictional_values` (and `source_value_extractions`) already use, so a code-floor-vs-best-practice delta is a plain numeric comparison rather than string parsing.
decisions/DR-2026-07-12-evidence-cell-state-schema-reconciliation.md:29:9. **Add the derived views**, with one correction to B's own sketch: `v_best_practice` must exclude `code_floor_only = 1` rows. `best-practices-assessment-system.md` §3's own hard rule states a Tier-6-only cell is `provisional`/`pending`, never the evidence basis for "best practice" — so a view that filters `state IN ('stated','provisional')` without also excluding `code_floor_only=1` would surface exactly the jurisdiction-code-as-best-practice conflation tier-system.md names as the failure mode this whole schema exists to prevent. `v_code_floor_only` is implemented as a join against the new `jurisdictional_values` table (not a bare self-filter), so the code-floor-delta surface `best-practices-assessment-system.md` §4 Phase 4 promises is actually computable from structured columns.
decisions/DR-2026-07-12-evidence-cell-state-schema-reconciliation.md:37:- `workplan/best-practices-assessment-system.md` §4's SQL sketch is superseded by the actual migration; its phasing plan (§8) is otherwise unaffected.
decisions/DR-2026-07-12-evidence-cell-state-schema-reconciliation.md:43:- **v1 (initial draft):** added `jurisdiction` to the table's `UNIQUE` key, added an unspecified `confidence_bucket` column, used unstructured `value_range TEXT`, and did not filter `code_floor_only` out of `v_best_practice`. Cited `D-0138`/`repo-strategy-revision-co.md` as settled in the companion architecture DR (see that DR's own revision history) and referenced this document's Tier-3 companion before it was written.
decisions/DR-2026-07-12-evidence-cell-state-schema-reconciliation.md:44:- **v2 (this version):** independent adversarial review found the jurisdiction-in-key choice reproduces the exact best-practice/code-floor conflation `tier-system.md` names as a failure mode, found `v_best_practice` would have surfaced `code_floor_only` rows as best-practice (a live bug, not a style note), found `confidence_bucket` and `value_range` under-specified, found the anti-hallucination and Tier-3 validator checks were deferred without being scoped as required follow-up, and found the item_code-identity rationale stale (relying on an outdated `bpc_source_slug` gap rather than the current, stronger `item_bpc_links` gap). All are corrected above. `decisions/DR-2026-07-12-tier3-stated-threshold.md` now exists and both its policy and validator implementation are complete.
decisions/DR-2026-07-12-tier3-stated-threshold.md:11:`decisions/DR-2026-05-29-evidence-hierarchy-reconciliation.md` redefined Tier 3 as "rarely the sole basis" for best-practice claims (now codified in `governance/tier-system.md` line 19: *"Supporting evidence for best-practice claims; rarely the sole basis"*), while flagging, explicitly unresolved:
decisions/DR-2026-07-12-tier3-stated-threshold.md:21:1. A cell whose only governing evidence is **T3-clinical** (with no Co-1/Co-2/T1/T2 corroboration) is `provisional`, not `stated` — consistent with `tier-system.md`'s "rarely the sole basis" characterization and with the general principle (already established for Tier 6 in `best-practices-assessment-system.md` §3's hard rule) that a determination's confidence should reflect the actual strength of its anchoring evidence, not just whether *some* evidence exists.
decisions/DR-2026-07-13-attestation-rule-identifier-registry-gap.md:20:| `best-practice-synthesis-routing` | 6 | The best-practice-vs-code-consensus routing rule (mission doctrine #2) |
decisions/DR-2026-07-13-attestation-rule-identifier-registry-gap.md:22:| `best-practice-supersession` | 3 | The DR-2026-05-24 supersession-check rule itself (self-referential in its own two attestations) |
decisions/DR-2026-07-13-value-genealogy-and-derivation-handshake.md:4:- Date: 2026-07-13 (authored in the evidence-architecture unification session, on the owner's directives: adjudicate best-practice-vs-consensus per mode; handle swept-path vs turning-radius, device-class heterogeneity, and multimodal width; fan out per population; decide whether a bottom-up/top-down handshake is required; harness the scattered md/yaml/json evidence body)
decisions/DR-2026-07-13-value-genealogy-and-derivation-handshake.md:6:- Affects (if ratified): `scripts/migrations/` (one follow-on migration), `workplan/best-practices-assessment-system.md` Phase 1 (extraction pass gains genealogy fields), `scripts/assess/assess_cell.py` (post-ratification: derivation-path gates), `references/fdr/` (naming + merge path), `governance/evidence-architecture.md` (gains §4.5 genealogy + §5.5 handshake on ratification)
decisions/DR-2026-07-13-value-genealogy-and-derivation-handshake.md:11:**Problem 1 (genealogy).** The project's central adjudication — best practice (dignity-bearing, most accommodating) vs consensus/precedent — currently has no computable form. The corridor-width genealogy proves the stakes: 1500mm turning "circles" in 24 jurisdictions trace to one 1970s anthropometric root (REF-00059/60: "based on research conducted in the 1970s… need to be updated"); the 1800mm passing consensus has **no traceable root anywhere in the corpus**; while 2440/2400mm has **two independent measurement/participatory roots** (ASL proxemics Co-1; swept-path anthropometry T3 entire-sample) plus an untraced regulatory convergence (MEXT T5 — a `committee_assertion` under this DR's own vocabulary until its derivation is mined). Precedent counts documents; evidence counts roots — and today nothing in the data layer can count roots. Worse, values are being compared across incommensurable **measurement paradigms** (static turning circle vs dynamic swept-path envelope — 97% of turns are asymmetric spin turns; scooters have no pivot at all) and across **device classes** (multiple codes self-declare their figures manual-wheelchair-only).
decisions/DR-2026-07-13-value-genealogy-and-derivation-handshake.md:21:Extend the (empty) B6 substrate with: `root_id` (shared identifier for one evidentiary root), `root_type` CHECK (`measurement_primary` / `participatory_finding` / `committee_assertion` / `derived_calculation` / `untraced`), `root_ref_id` (FK to `evidence_sources` when the root document is in corpus), `echo_of` (transmission-chain note), `measurement_paradigm` CHECK (`swept_path_dynamic` / `static_turning_circle` / `static_clearance` / `anthropometric_percentile` / `instrumented_physical_measurement` — acoustic/photometric/force values / `route_metric` — distances, intervals / `field_observation` / `participatory_spatial` / `stated_unmeasured`), `device_class` CHECK (`manual_self_propelled` / `manual_attendant` / `power_chair` / `scooter` / `bariatric_manual` / `bariatric_power` — the corpus itself distinguishes them (REF-00061; FDR-BAB-04) / `walker_rollator` / `mixed` / `not_device_scoped`), `root_population_note` (the root's sample description — the fit-population test), `file_anchor` (path+section into the md/yaml/json corpus — the tri-format provenance link). Derived view `v_value_independence`: per (parameter, population), COUNT(DISTINCT root_id) excluding `committee_assertion` — **the computable best-practice-vs-consensus discriminator** — under three anti-gaming disciplines (adversarial-review hardening): (a) **root registry**: a `root_id` must reference either a `root_ref_id` in `evidence_sources` or a registered external-root stub (one row per out-of-corpus root, e.g. the 1970s VA/HUD studies), so two extractors cannot mint two ids for one root and double the count; (b) **`untraced` rows carry NULL `root_id`** and are excluded from the count — untraceability can never out-score a traced chain; (c) **`root_classification_basis` + `contested` fields** per row, so the root-vs-echo judgment is recordably disputable, not free-text folklore.
decisions/DR-2026-07-20-evidence-architecture-weighted-strength-reconciliation.md:15:- `tier-system.md §8` (:89–99): *"Every tier can anchor a best-practice claim; the claim's strength is weighted by the tier of its evidence"* — three strength bands via `●◐○`; T4/T5 anchor at `◐` ("current standards practice"), T6/grey at `○` (weak, code-floor).
decisions/DR-2026-07-20-evidence-architecture-weighted-strength-reconciliation.md:22:| §2 (:44) | regulatory stratum sources "do not anchor best-practice claims … convergence of codes is convergence-not-evidence" |
decisions/DR-2026-07-20-evidence-architecture-weighted-strength-reconciliation.md:24:| §5 (:103) | a `regulatory_stratum_only` determination "is never rendered as best practice, in any register, for any audience. `v_best_practice` excludes it." |
decisions/DR-2026-07-20-evidence-architecture-weighted-strength-reconciliation.md:25:| §6 invariant **I3** (:139) | "No best-practice language on regulatory-stratum-only cells, in any register, under any weighting profile." |
decisions/DR-2026-07-20-evidence-architecture-weighted-strength-reconciliation.md:30:- `scripts/assess/assess_cell.py:~554` — `CREATE VIEW v_best_practice … WHERE state IN ('stated','provisional') AND code_floor_only = 0 AND tier_basis NOT LIKE '%(regulatory_stratum_only)'`.
decisions/DR-2026-07-20-evidence-architecture-weighted-strength-reconciliation.md:34:**Precedence is not ambiguous.** `evidence-architecture.md:4` carries the clause "where this document and a cited source ever diverge, the cited source governs," and `tier-system.md §8` post-dates the 2026-07-13 ratification. So **in the interim `tier-system.md §8` governs**: every tier may anchor at graded strength *today*. The divergence is therefore not a live behavioral contradiction in doctrine — it is an **unreconciled-text + stale-code** state: the canonical architecture doc and the `v_best_practice` view still describe and enforce the superseded wall.
decisions/DR-2026-07-20-evidence-architecture-weighted-strength-reconciliation.md:36:The one substantive thing precedence does **not** silently fix: `v_best_practice` still *mechanically excludes* regulatory-stratum-only cells. Code behavior and §8 already disagree the moment such a cell would be rendered.
decisions/DR-2026-07-20-evidence-architecture-weighted-strength-reconciliation.md:40:`tier-system.md §8`'s weighted-strength model can be read two ways where it meets `evidence-architecture.md §5/§6`. The owner must pick one, and the choice is genuinely load-bearing because it decides whether a code-only cell can ever carry best-practice framing:
decisions/DR-2026-07-20-evidence-architecture-weighted-strength-reconciliation.md:42:### Option A — Weak-anchor: regulatory-stratum cells enter the best-practice surface at the weak band, with mandatory honesty flags
decisions/DR-2026-07-20-evidence-architecture-weighted-strength-reconciliation.md:43:§8 is read as fully repealing the anchoring gate. A `regulatory_stratum_only` cell becomes a `○`-strength best-practice determination — surfaced, but always labelled weak/code-floor and carrying the anti-laundering language.
decisions/DR-2026-07-20-evidence-architecture-weighted-strength-reconciliation.md:48:- `evidence-architecture.md §5` (:103): drop "never rendered as best practice, in any register"; replace with the weak-band rendering rule.
decisions/DR-2026-07-20-evidence-architecture-weighted-strength-reconciliation.md:49:- `evidence-architecture.md §6` **I3** (:139): **repeal the absolute form** — I3 becomes "no *unflagged* / no *strong-band* best-practice language on regulatory-stratum-only cells," not "no best-practice language at all." Re-check I5 for consistency.
decisions/DR-2026-07-20-evidence-architecture-weighted-strength-reconciliation.md:50:- Register map row 3 (:130): allow weak-band best-practice phrasing alongside the convergence-not-evidence caveat.
decisions/DR-2026-07-20-evidence-architecture-weighted-strength-reconciliation.md:51:- `assess_cell.py` `v_best_practice`: drop (or reweight) the `regulatory_stratum_only` exclusion; add a strength-band column so the weak band is queryably distinct.
decisions/DR-2026-07-20-evidence-architecture-weighted-strength-reconciliation.md:53:### Option B — Rendering-strength-only: §8 governs *how strongly* an already-anchored cell is rendered, and regulatory-stratum-only cells stay excluded from `v_best_practice`
decisions/DR-2026-07-20-evidence-architecture-weighted-strength-reconciliation.md:54:§8's "every tier can anchor" is read as applying within the evidence-anchored population determination (grading confidence of T1/T2/T3-backed values), while a cell whose **entire** basis is T4–T6 remains a Universal-Mode regulatory determination that is not a best-practice claim. The wall stands for *code-only* cells; the weighting applies to *evidence-backed* cells.
decisions/DR-2026-07-20-evidence-architecture-weighted-strength-reconciliation.md:57:- `evidence-architecture.md`: **no change to §5/§6/I3 or `v_best_practice`.** Add a clause to §2/§6 that scopes §8's weighting to anchored cells and explicitly preserves I3 for `regulatory_stratum_only`.
decisions/DR-2026-07-20-evidence-architecture-weighted-strength-reconciliation.md:58:- `tier-system.md §8`: add a scoping sentence that T4/T5's `◐` "current standards practice" rendering is *standards-practice* framing, not *best-practice* framing, for cells with no evidence-tier anchor — closing the apparent contradiction from the tier-system side.
decisions/DR-2026-07-20-evidence-architecture-weighted-strength-reconciliation.md:62:Both options edit a **ratified canonical document** (`evidence-architecture.md`) and one repeals or rescopes a **ratified integrity invariant** (I3) and changes a determination-surface view. That is doctrine, not hygiene. Per the governance model, canonical docs are "edited only after ratification," and the choice between A and B is a values call about whether a code-only requirement may ever wear best-practice language — precisely the "convergence-is-not-evidence" concern I3 was built to protect. It is the owner's to make.
decisions/DR-2026-07-20-intra-category-cross-test.md:3:- Status: **ACCEPTED — owner ratification "Yes, ratify ALL recent work", 2026-07-21; forks X2 (functional-neighbourhood granularity) and X5 (gate strength) accepted as drafted; execution (cross_test_pairs migration + connection-discovery `--mode category-crosstest` + assess_cell ICCT gate) staged per `decisions/RATIFICATION-RECORD-2026-07-21.md` §Addendum.** Authored on owner directive 2026-07-20 ("ensure that our work in deriving best practices includes a step whereby every item/specification within a category gets tested against the other items in that same category… considering these items beyond script prescription / silos by title / too-specific topics").
decisions/DR-2026-07-20-intra-category-cross-test.md:6:- Affects (if ratified): one follow-on migration (a `cross_test_pairs` worklist table + `v_cross_test_open` view); `skills/connection-discovery_SKILL.md` (gains `--mode category-crosstest`); `scripts/assess/assess_cell.py` (post-ratification: an ICCT gate in the `stated` predicate, under a new `rule_version`); `workplan/best-practices-assessment-system.md` §3 (the determination algorithm gains a cross-item step); companion demonstration `references/methodology/intra-category-cross-test-methodology.md`.
decisions/DR-2026-07-20-intra-category-cross-test.md:13:The best-practices assessment engine (`workplan/best-practices-assessment-system.md`; live in `evidence_cell_state`) assesses each **cell = (item_code × population × design_scale)** on its own evidence. DR-2026-07-13 H1 counts *roots, paradigms and device-classes within a cell*; H2 counts *derivation paths into a cell*. Both look **inward**. Nothing in the pipeline requires a determination to be tested against the **other items in its own category** before it ships.
decisions/DR-2026-07-20-intra-category-cross-test.md:93:So, on readiness: the *method* for cross-mode best-practice adjudication is ratified (DR-2026-07-13) and demonstrated on the hardest cell (E-08); the *substrate* is live (genealogy fields + `v_value_independence`; the determination engine has produced its first 13 cells across Universal and Population scale). We can begin — and have. The ICCT is the **missing required step** that makes "begin" safe to scale: without it, corpus-wide determination would ship title-siloed cells at exactly the moment the engine turns 13 hand-checked cells into ~1,800 machine-checked ones.
